  "taxCfPending": "Pending loss",
  "taxHowRules": "The same sales, on a FIFO basis instead of AVCO, which is what the Bizkaia foral tax return (NF 13/2013) requires and not what the Sales tab uses. A loss with a repurchase in the two months before or after is deferred under Art. 43 (letter g for homogeneous securities and, for transmissions from 1 January 2025, letter i for crypto assets of the same type), in the proportion repurchased, and computes when the repurchased units are transmitted; offsetting against earlier years follows Art. 66. The repurchase arithmetic follows the DGT rulings V1403-21, V1117-21 and V3282-18 on the parallel state rule, which do not bind the Hacienda Foral.",
  "taxHowOwnRules": "In a swap, the transmission value is the greater of the two sides (Art. 47.1.i and 47.1.p). Quoin's own criteria, not the norm's nor the DGT's: the acquisition value of what is received is that same value, a reasoned criterion the norm does not state literally; a repurchased unit counts for one sale only, oldest sale first; the units that receive a deferral are taken in order of purchase, oldest to newest, then those bought after the sale; and within one purchase, the deferral is spread equally over the units still held.",
  "taxNoRate": "No exchange rate: {names}. Their trades could not be converted to euros and are not part of this calculation. Check them before using these figures in a tax return.",
  "taxUnclassified": "No repurchase rule: {names}. Its type (bond, commodity or cash) is neither a listed security nor a crypto asset: a bond held directly yields income from movable capital, to which the repurchase rule does not apply, and a commodity held directly would have a rule of its own, which Quoin does not model. Its sales are computed with no repurchase rule. Check them before using these figures in a tax return.",
